tasks.prompt:
A garden record stores plant details:

```
{
  "plants": [
    {"species": "rose", "height": 1.45, "watered": true},
    {"species": "fern", "height": 0.8, "watered": false}
  ]
}
```

Write a program that prints the full key path of every leaf value. For each plant print one line per field in order species, height, watered:

Line format: `plants[0].species = rose`

For Text print the value unquoted, for Real print with 1 decimal place, for Bool print `true` or `false`.

Print exactly 6 lines. No trailing spaces.

A community garden stores soil readings for each plot as a JSON document like {"plot":"P1","ph":6.5,"moisture":42,"sun":"full"}. Below are five plots as JSON documents.

Plot JSON documents:
{"plot":"P1","ph":6.5,"moisture":42,"sun":"full"}
{"plot":"P2","ph":7.1,"moisture":35,"sun":"part"}
{"plot":"P3","ph":5.9,"moisture":51,"sun":"shade"}
{"plot":"P4","ph":6.8,"moisture":44,"sun":"full"}
{"plot":"P5","ph":7.4,"moisture":29,"sun":"part"}

Output one line per plot in the order given, in the exact format:
<plot> pH=<ph, one decimal place> MOIST=<moisture> SUN=<sun>
After all plots, output one line:
ACIDIC COUNT <number of plots with ph strictly less than 6.5>
